XB-Original-Maintainer: NVIDIA <cudatools@nvidia.com>
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: NVIDIA's 580 kernel modules (DKMS) for Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards
 This package builds the NVIDIA binary kernel modules needed by
 nvidia-driver, using DKMS.
 Provided that you have the kernel header packages installed, the kernel
 module will be built for your running kernel and automatically rebuilt for
 any new kernel headers that are installed.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS: NVIDIA's nvidia-kernel-dkms ${nvidia:Version}, unmodified,
 for the cards the edition's open modules (Turing and newer) do not run:
 NVIDIA's 580 branch is the last that supports Maxwell, Pascal and Volta.
 NVIDIA's display code is closed in this driver, so it has none of the
 edition's HDMI 3D and deep colour patches; Stereo KWin's other outputs
 (anaglyph, interleaved, side by side and top and bottom for screens
 switched by hand, output pairs) work on it. nouveau keeps the edition's
 HDMI 3D on these cards, at lower speed: Hardware Setup offers both.

Package: sparky-stereo-nvidia-legacy-580xx-driver-lock
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: Keep NVIDIA's driver at the version of the 580 kernel module
 An APT preferences file, generated from this package's version, that keeps
 every NVIDIA driver package at ${nvidia:Version}, the version
 nvidia-legacy-580xx-kernel-dkms is built for, and never installs another
 NVIDIA kernel module package. It sorts before
 sparky-stereo-nvidia-driver-lock's file and names the same packages, so it
 decides while it is installed: a newer driver from NVIDIA's repositories,
 which no longer runs Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards, cannot replace the
 580 driver.
 .
 NVIDIA's 580 user space for these cards comes from the edition's
 repository: NVIDIA publishes it for Debian only in its repository for
 Debian 12, whose key Debian 14's APT refuses (a SHA-1 binding signature).
 See README.Debian.
